Here's an example JavaScript code to compute the net present value (NPV) of the given information:
```
// Set the variables
const discountRate = 0.06;
const cashFlow = -1000;
const years = 15;
// Calculate the NPV
let npv = 0;
for (let i = 1; i <= years; i++) {
  npv += cashFlow / Math.pow(1 + discountRate, i);
}
// Round the NPV to 2 decimal places
