// Output the result
console.log(`The net present value is $${npv}`);
```
The code uses a for loop to iterate through each year and calculate the present value of the cash flow using the formula `PV = CF / (1 + r)^n`, where `PV` is the present value, `CF` is the cash flow, `r` is the discount rate, and `n` is the year. The present values are then summed to get the NPV. The code rounds the NPV to 2 decimal places using the `Math.round()` function and outputs the result to the console.

