One way to group the given list of countries based on their location is to create a HashMap with keys representing the continents and values representing ArrayLists of countries. We can then iterate through the list of countries and add each country to the appropriate ArrayList based on its continent.
Here's some Java code that accomplishes this:
```
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.HashMap;
public class CountryGrouper {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Given list of countries
        String[] countries = {"France", "India", "Italy", "Japan"};

        // Create HashMap to group countries by continent
        HashMap<String, ArrayList<String>> continentGroups = new HashMap<>();
        continentGroups.put("Europe", new ArrayList<String>());
        continentGroups.put("Asia", new ArrayList<String>());
        continentGroups.put("North America", new ArrayList<String>());
        continentGroups.put("South America", new ArrayList<String>());
        continentGroups.put("Africa", new ArrayList<String>());
        continentGroups.put("Australia", new ArrayList<String>());

        // Add each country to appropriate continent group
        for (String country : countries) {
            if (country.equals("France") || country.equals("Italy")) {
                continentGroups.get("Europe").add(country);
            } else if (country.equals("India") || country.equals("Japan")) {
                continentGroups.get("Asia").add(country);
            }
            // Add other countries and continents as needed
        }

        // Print out each group of countries
        for (String continent : continentGroups.keySet()) {
            System.out.println(continent + ": " + continentGroups.get(continent));
        }
    }
}
```
This code creates a HashMap with keys representing the continents and values representing ArrayLists of countries. It then adds each country to the appropriate ArrayList based on its continent using a series of if-else statements. Finally, it prints out each group of countries. 
Note that this code assumes that each continent has an equal number of countries. If this is not the case, you may need to modify the code to handle uneven groups.

