How can I calculate the correlation coefficient between employee performance and HR management practices using Java? I have a data set containing employee performance evaluation scores and HR data such as recruitment, training, and compensation. Can you provide me with a Java code to calculate the correlation coefficient and interpret the result?
Here's a Java code that uses the Pearson Correlation Coefficient method to calculate the correlation between two variables:
import java.util.*;
public class Correlation {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.println("Enter the number of data points: ");
        int n = sc.nextInt();
        double[] x = new double[n];
        double[] y = new double[n];
        System.out.println("Enter the values of x: ");
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            x[i] = sc.nextDouble();
        }
        System.out.println("Enter the values of y: ");
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            y[i] = sc.nextDouble();
        }
        double sum_x = 0.0;
        double sum_y = 0.0;
        double sum_xy = 0.0;
        double sum_x2 = 0.0;
        double sum_y2 = 0.0;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            sum_x += x[i];
            sum_y += y[i];
            sum_xy += x[i] * y[i];
            sum_x2 += Math.pow(x[i], 2);
            sum_y2 += Math.pow(y[i], 2);
        }
        double numerator = n * sum_xy - sum_x * sum_y;
        double denominator = Math.sqrt((n * sum_x2 - Math.pow(sum_x, 2)) * (n * sum_y2 - Math.pow(sum_y, 2)));
        double correlation = numerator / denominator;
        System.out.println("The correlation coefficient between employee performance and HR management practices is: " + correlation);
    }
}
To interpret the result, a correlation coefficient of +1 indicates a perfect positive correlation, 0 indicates no correlation, and -1 indicates a perfect negative correlation. A correlation coefficient between 0 and +1 or 0 and -1 indicates a weak to moderate correlation.

