How can I use PHP code to identify sentences in present perfect tense that describe completed actions relevant to the present? Can you provide an example of such a sentence and one that describes a habitual action in the present?
To achieve this, you can use the PHP library called "php-nlp-tools" and its "POS" (part-of-speech) tagging function to identify verb tenses. Here's an example code snippet:
```
// Load the library
require_once 'vendor/autoload.php';
// Set up the POS tagger
$pos = new \NlpTools\Analysis\Pos();
// Define the sentences to test
$sentences = [
    "I have finished my homework.",
    "I finish my homework every day.",
];
// Loop through the sentences and determine their tense
foreach ($sentences as $sentence) {
    // Tokenize the sentence
    $tokens = explode(' ', $sentence);
    // Tag the parts of speech
    $tags = $pos->tag($tokens);
    // Find the verb and its tense
    foreach ($tags as $index => $tag) {
        if ($tag['pos'] === 'VBP' && $tags[$index+1]['pos'] === 'VBN') {
            echo "{$sentence} is in present perfect tense.\n";
            break;
        } else if ($tag['pos'] === 'VB' && $tags[$index+1]['pos'] === 'VBZ') {
            echo "{$sentence} describes a habitual action in the present.\n";
            break;
        }
    }
}
```
This code uses the "VBP" and "VBN" tags to identify the present perfect tense and the "VB" and "VBZ" tags to identify habitual actions in the present. Here's an example output:
