                if($result % 2 != 0 && $result < $smallest_odd) {
                    $smallest_odd = $result;
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
if($smallest_odd == PHP_INT_MAX) {
    echo "No odd integer found.";
} else {
    echo "The smallest odd integer that can be obtained by adding the product and sum of two prime numbers, where the difference between the two prime numbers is less than 10, is: " . $smallest_odd;
}
```
The code first defines a function `isPrime()` to check if a number is prime or not. It then initializes a variable `$smallest_odd` to the maximum integer value, which will be used to keep track of the smallest odd integer found so far.
The code then loops through all prime numbers less than 100, and for each prime number it loops through all prime numbers greater than it and less than 100, where the difference between the two prime numbers is less than 10. For each pair of prime numbers, it calculates the product and sum, adds them together, and checks if the result is odd and smaller than the current smallest odd integer found so far. If it is, it updates the value of `$smallest_odd`.
Finally, the code checks if a smallest odd integer was found and prints the result accordingly.

